॰                        --entry सेतुः मुख्य  पारम्.t1 सेतुः.t1`
॰                       -> `0 source(s) failed to compile, 3 object(s) linked`,
॰                          45,368,677 steps, 65,832 octets of ELF. This is run 1
॰                          above RE-RUN with the import present, and it reads
॰                          exactly what run 3's inline control read.
॰   c  NATIVE RUN       `yantra-run` on that image
॰                       -> `halt: Finisher { value: 2765619, status: Some(42) }`
॰   d  INLINE CONTROL   `निजम्.t1` built and run the same way
॰                       -> 2 objects, 42,531,668 steps, 65,776 octets, and
॰                          `Finisher { value: 2765619, status: Some(42) }` —
॰                          THE IDENTICAL FINISHER WORD, not merely the same
॰                          status. The cross-module call and the inline
॰                          arithmetic are indistinguishable at the halt.
॰   e  NEGATIVE CONTROL the caller built ALONE, callee object withheld
॰                       -> `0 failed to compile, 2 object(s) linked`, then
॰                          `STOPPED AT link: the product returned an empty
॰                          image` with `link refusals` naming this module's
॰                          own text. So the callee's object is LOAD-BEARING:
॰                          run c did not reach ४२ by computing it here.
॰
॰ AND THE SYMBOL QUESTION THE PREVIOUS CYCLE LEFT OPEN IS CLOSED, FOR PENNIES,
॰ BEFORE ANY IMAGE WAS BUILT. It asked whether the emitter writes a callee
॰ target carrying the CALLER's module prefix — `tools/demo.sh` had reported
॰ `1 call (0 cross-module)` and a target spelled `सेतुःसंज्ञा२०००००१य्`. It does
॰ not. `T1_BOOT_TEXT` on both halves of the pair, on this tree:
॰   this file emits  `लङ्घनम् पुनःस्थानम्म् पारम्द्विगुणयय् ।`
॰   `पारम्.t1` emits `॥ वैश्विकम् पारम्द्विगुणय ॥`
॰ — the callee's own exported global, spelled the same, no caller prefix. The
॰ `ॱ` of `पारम्ॱद्विगुणय` is flattened away on both sides, which is why they
॰ meet. That dump costs one `--object` run and answers what an image answers.
॰
॰ WHAT IS STILL NOT DONE, SAID PLAINLY. No RUNG 101 was written: a rung pairs an
॰ INTERPRETED prediction with a NATIVE status, and `t1_image` prints
॰ `predict: interpreted सेतुःॱमुख्य refused: no routine named … is loaded` for
॰ both halves of the pair AND for the `निजम्` control — `--compiler` supplies
॰ the loader's sources and `spec/rung/` is not among them, so the interpreted
॰ side of this pair has never been run and there is no prediction to embed yet.
॰ That is the next unit and it is a `त1_image` loader question, not a compiler
॰ one. The member `द्विगुणय` also remains taken on trust at resolve
॰ (`artha.t1:2946`); the LINKER is what refused it in run e, not `अर्थ`.

॰ THE ONE LINE THE FOUR RUNS ABOVE WERE MISSING. `पारम्ॱद्विगुणय` names a
॰ module, and `अर्थ` resolves the MODULE half against this file's own scope —
॰ so without this declaration the name has none, exactly as the Rust twin
॰ said in words. The member `द्विगुणय` is still taken on trust; that gap is
॰ `अर्थ`'s, is documented at `artha.t1:2946`, and is not this file's.
आयातः पारम् ।

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः मुख्य ददाति न६४ आदि
